            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Lead with the Conclusion: Don't Waste Cold Start Budget on New Acquisition</h2>
<p>If you've just launched your DTC site with a monthly ad budget of $5,000 to $20,000, my first recommendation is: <strong>allocate at least 60% of your budget to retargeting, not cold traffic acquisition.</strong></p>
<p>This isn't theory—it's a pattern we've repeatedly verified after working with dozens of cross-border DTC sellers.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Why Burning Budget on Cold Traffic is the Least Efficient Approach</h2>
<p>A new site has zero purchase data, user behavior data, and minimal Pixel accumulation. When you run cold traffic campaigns under these conditions, the platform can only use limited targeting data to learn your audience model—resulting in poor performance, high costs, and slow account权重 building.</p>
<p>One tool-category DTC seller reported investing $15,000 in Meta cold-start campaigns during their first month, achieving an ROAS of only 0.8—far below the 1.5 break-even threshold. The problem wasn't ad creative; their Pixel had zero conversion data, and the algorithm simply couldn't generate an effective model.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The core contradiction of cold start: <strong>The more data you lack, the more you need data to optimize; but without data, your budget keeps draining.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Budget Allocation by Stage</h2>
<h3>Phase 1: Cold Start (0-3 Months)</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Objective</th>
<th>Budget Allocation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Retargeting (Site Visitors)</td>
<td>60-70%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Lookalike Audiences</td>
<td>20-25%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cold Start Testing</td>
<td>10-15%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Strategic Focus:</strong><br />
- Prioritize accumulating first batch of visitors through organic content, SEO, or paid referral traffic<br />
- Retarget this visitor pool multiple times to increase conversion probability<br />
- Retargeting conversion data will reverse-optimize your Pixel model, building foundation for scale</p>
<h3>Phase 2: Growth Stage (3-6 Months)</h3>
<p>Once retargeting ROAS stabilizes above 2.5 and your Pixel has accumulated 500+ conversion events, gradually increase cold start budget.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Objective</th>
<th>Budget Allocation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Retargeting</td>
<td>40-50%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Lookalike Scaling</td>
<td>25-30%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cold Start Testing</td>
<td>20-30%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Phase 3: Maturity (6+ Months)</h3>
<p>Once your account model stabilizes, shift budget focus toward scalable acquisition while maintaining sufficient retargeting spend to boost customer lifetime value (LTV).</p>
<hr />
<h2>Prioritize Your Platform Budget Allocation</h2>
<p>Not all traffic channels suit cold start campaigns. Our operations experience shows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Google Search Ads</strong>: Ideal for capturing purchase-intent traffic; more effective for cold start than Meta</li>
<li><strong>Meta (Facebook/Instagram)</strong>: Highly dependent on Pixel data and audience modeling; lower cold start efficiency</li>
<li><strong>TikTok</strong>: Still in traffic dividend period, but longer conversion paths; suitable for testing non-mainstream categories</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> During cold start, prioritize testing Google Search ads for precise keywords to accumulate first conversion data, then use that data to amplify Meta retargeting.</p>
<hr />
<h2>One Critical Benchmark</h2>
<p>If your retargeting ROAS consistently stays below 1.5, the problem is usually not budget allocation but:</p>
<ol>
<li>Poor landing page experience—users arrive but don't convert</li>
<li>Retargeting frequency too high, causing audience fatigue</li>
<li>Audience segmentation insufficient—high-value and low-intent users mixed together</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Optimization sequence should be: refine audience and creative first, then reconsider budget reallocation.</strong></p>
<hr />
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>The core logic of DTC site advertising is <strong>using retargeting data to feed the algorithm, and using algorithmic efficiency to lower customer acquisition costs.</strong> Allocating budget to cold acquisition during cold start essentially means buying the platform's learning time with money—high cost, low efficiency.</p>
<p>Remember this allocation principle: <strong>Data first, scale second.</strong></p>
